{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits","id":1008606,"title":"Trouble with Spirits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-26T10:50:20-08:00","id":1008606,"title":"Trouble with Spirits","content":"Hello! I don't usually write in forums. In fact, I've only created an account pretty recently, even though I play Storytelling games for some years now.<br /> In any case, I was having some trouble with things related to spirits in Werewolf:<br /> a) What exactly happens when a spirit is destroyed? I can picture a tree dying if it's spirit is destroyed, but what about, say, a knife?<br /> b) Is every spirit a reflection of something in the material world? Every oak-spirit on the spirit wilds, and every bear-spirit has a material counterpart? If so, how far away from it's material counterpart can a spirit go?<br /> c) This is minor, but I can't help but wonder, how much does a Claimed person appearence shift? Or is that up to the ST?<br /> <br /> Thank you all in advance, have a pleasant day!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T12:10:51-08:00","id":1008638,"title":"","content":"Alright, lets see if I can help:<br /> <br /> a) Spirits and their material analogues aren't quite as linked as that. If a spirit dies nothing drastic happens to it's counterpart. It just feels a bit lifeless and dull, generally until another one starts hanging round it.<br /> <br /> b)Spirits can outlive their material counterparts. Younger, weak spirits usually hang around the thing that spawned them but they don't have to and more powerful ones usually don't. In fact, often a spirit is awoken by their material counterpart's destruction. <br /> <br /> c)A claimed's appearance is mostly a product if the dread powers they manifest. This can be as subtle or as blatant as you like, but as a general rule more powerful spirits warp their hosts more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T12:20:37-08:00","id":1008640,"title":"","content":"I think I got it, thanks a lot!<br /> So, just to be sure, if I have, say, a dog, this dog spawned a &quot;dog-spirit&quot; when it was born, or it would only spawn something when someone started feeling some affection for it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T12:21:54-08:00","id":1008642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1008640#post1008640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I got it, thanks a lot!<br /> So, just to be sure, if I have, say, a dog, this dog spawned a &quot;dog-spirit&quot; when it was born, or it would only spawn something when someone started feeling some affection for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>They'd probably just be motes of dog-essence unless something happened to wake them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T12:22:39-08:00","id":1008643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1008642#post1008642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They'd probably just be motes of dog-essence unless something happened to wake them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T16:10:15-08:00","id":1008706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits#post1008606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">b) Is every spirit a reflection of something in the material world? Every oak-spirit on the spirit wilds, and every bear-spirit has a material counterpart? If so, how far away from it's material counterpart can a spirit go?</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything has a spirit, but not everything is awake. If it's not awake, the potential for it's spirit remains bound in the material counterpart, the process of awakening tends to be gradual, sudden awakenings are traumatic.<br /> <br /> The Shadow is a place in which memory and symbolism takes a heavy part in it's metaphysics. You can use the Spirit Whispers Facet on a recently built computer and ask for it's login information, because it has a spirit, even if it's not awake. It's like having a thing whisper in it's sleep.<br /> <br /> Back to the subject of awakening, you'll often see cars without a will of their own following their material counterparts around the spiritscape of a city. The awakened ones prey on them.<br /> <br /> Slumbering spirit animals show up as signs of the animals presence. Birds nests, predator's dens, tracks.<br /> <br /> Conceptual spirits in their slumber impregnate a location with their feelings, in a natural way. Someplace feels creepy, another seems awe-inspiring, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T18:39:19-08:00","id":1008738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1008706#post1008706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everything has a spirit, but not everything is awake. If it's not awake, the potential for it's spirit remains bound in the material counterpart, the process of awakening tends to be gradual, sudden awakenings are traumatic.<br /> <br /> The Shadow is a place in which memory and symbolism takes a heavy part in it's metaphysics. You can use the Spirit Whispers Facet on a recently built computer and ask for it's login information, because it has a spirit, even if it's not awake. It's like having a thing whisper in it's sleep.<br /> <br /> Back to the subject of awakening, you'll often see cars without a will of their own following their material counterparts around the spiritscape of a city. The awakened ones prey on them.<br /> <br /> Slumbering spirit animals show up as signs of the animals presence. Birds nests, predator's dens, tracks.<br /> <br /> Conceptual spirits in their slumber impregnate a location with their feelings, in a natural way. Someplace feels creepy, another seems awe-inspiring, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>And how exactly would one awake a spirit?<br /> I'm sure it says somewhere in the books, I'm sorry, I didn't really catch-up on my supplements, been focused on the 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T23:38:50-08:00","id":1008835,"title":"","content":"Magic, or Essence.<br /> <br /> It gets Essence when its Resonance is acted upon or it gets attention. A few other things. A car suddenly appreciated more, polished and fixed up might awaken its shadow-self. A spirit of anger gone dormant in a house might awaken when someone inside stubs their toe, then begin a spree of anger-spurring urging in order to glut itself.<br /> <br /> By 'magic' I mean there are abilities throughout the supernaturals that deal with spirits that allow them to awaken or empower spirits. It's not inconceivable a once-powerful spirit might have a rite or something that would grant it enough Essence to waken it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-27-2016, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T01:42:17-08:00","id":1008860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1008835#post1008835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magic, or Essence.<br /> <br /> It gets Essence when its Resonance is acted upon or it gets attention. A few other things. A car suddenly appreciated more, polished and fixed up might awaken its shadow-self. A spirit of anger gone dormant in a house might awaken when someone inside stubs their toe, then begin a spree of anger-spurring urging in order to glut itself.<br /> <br /> By 'magic' I mean there are abilities throughout the supernaturals that deal with spirits that allow them to awaken or empower spirits. It's not inconceivable a once-powerful spirit might have a rite or something that would grant it enough Essence to waken it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow that gives me a lot of ideas, what a cool concept. Thanks for explaining it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T04:01:02-08:00","id":1008873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1008738#post1008738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And how exactly would one awake a spirit?<br /> I'm sure it says somewhere in the books, I'm sorry, I didn't really catch-up on my supplements, been focused on the 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Make up a rite for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T04:28:58-08:00","id":1008879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1008873#post1008873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Make up a rite for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I got it. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T13:05:50-08:00","id":1009445,"title":"","content":"Mind if I add a few other questions? I also feel as though I don't quite &quot;get&quot; spirits... or I do, but to an extreme degree. And I'm going to reveal the depth of my ignorance here, so laugh and bear with me please.<br /> <br /> My impression from reading the books is that spirits (awake ones, per thread) exist in a purely predatory state all the time--they don't sleep again, reproduce, create, etc.: they only eat and grow. Kinda like insects if they never had to stop and breed.<br /> <br /> Now all this, to me, leads to several problems that I feel I'm just missing something on:<br /> <br /> 1. &quot;Food&quot; supply--wouldn't an awakened spirit consume anything and everything around itself in rather short order, in an ever-widening spiral until it can't find another spirit of any size? What keeps the spirits in any semblance of an ecology at all? Spirit-feudal arrangements tithing essence are all fine and good, but why bother? Spirits don't seem very cooperative AT ALL, so who needs the feudalism? It just seems as though the natural state of Twilight should be &quot;blasted spirit wasteland with a few motes no-one noticed yet.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2. If I'm just wrong (highly possible), and spirits DO lean toward moderation in some way (they get injured and sleep, they consume mainly/only same type, etc.) then you could have a kind of ecology, of sorts, in which various spirits mill around waiting for essence of the right flavor to come along or they get hungry enough to eat something weird. But what prods them toward social organization (feudalism again)? Do they naturally order themselves hierarchically? What keeps the world from being eventually flooded by Rank 5 spirits?<br /> <br /> 3. Ok, essence is generated in the material when a similar resonance is acted on. Cool, ok. But even very young spirits quickly realize where essence comes from (material), that it is generated by material things/creatures/people, and that said things/creatures/people are MUCH more likely to generate the best essence if they are compelled to do so. Which spirits can accomplish. So what keeps them from just urging everything/one in sight, rolling attempts until they make it? Because as far as I can tell an urged [person] is pretty much F'ed and will eventually end up Claimed and totally under the control of the spirit--their free-will a forgotten, discarded shell to the alien intelligence.<br /> <br /> So... correct me here, please.<br /> <br /> Because from this perspective nothing in the CofD looks more burn-it-with-fire terrifying than the spirits and the inevitability of their plague on mankind.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> PS. Ok, the answer can be &quot;Uratha!&quot; and that's why The Wolf must Hunt, sure, but they're relatively few in number and always were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T14:15:01-08:00","id":1009476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1009445#post1009445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. &amp;quot;Food&amp;quot; supply--wouldn't an awakened spirit consume anything and everything around itself in rather short order, in an ever-widening spiral until it can't find another spirit of any size? What keeps the spirits in any semblance of an ecology at all? Spirit-feudal arrangements tithing essence are all fine and good, but why bother? Spirits don't seem very cooperative AT ALL, so who needs the feudalism? It just seems as though the natural state of Twilight should be &amp;quot;blasted spirit wasteland with a few motes no-one noticed yet.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits are restricted in what they can eat. Essence (or other spirits) they consume must be of conceptually linked resonance to their own nature. They'll only consume incompatible Essence in extremely dire circumstances. Granted, their nature will broaden as they grow more powerful, and that does create a sort of spiral like you describe, but spirits with incompatible resonance are generally safe from each other. Also, re: spirits being pure predatory instinct, I don't think that's really true. Spirits are as their nature dictates, so Predator spirits are predatory, but like an agriculture spirit probably wouldn't be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1009445#post1009445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. If I'm just wrong (highly possible), and spirits DO lean toward moderation in some way (they get injured and sleep, they consume mainly/only same type, etc.) then you could have a kind of ecology, of sorts, in which various spirits mill around waiting for essence of the right flavor to come along or they get hungry enough to eat something weird. But what prods them toward social organization (feudalism again)? Do they naturally order themselves hierarchically? What keeps the world from being eventually flooded by Rank 5 spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Higher Rank spirits find it more difficult to cross the Gauntlet and to exist in the physical world for extended periods of time. As for why the feudal behavior, it's simply the most efficient way for more powerful spirits to fulfill their Essence needs. They're too big to cross the Gauntlet easily and require too much Essence for sustainence to get by exclusively on eating other Spirits - they would quickly end up exhausting their own food source. So, they give weaker spirits access to their territory in exchange for Essence tithes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1009445#post1009445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Ok, essence is generated in the material when a similar resonance is acted on. Cool, ok. But even very young spirits quickly realize where essence comes from (material), that it is generated by material things/creatures/people, and that said things/creatures/people are MUCH more likely to generate the best essence if they are compelled to do so. Which spirits can accomplish. So what keeps them from just urging everything/one in sight, rolling attempts until they make it? Because as far as I can tell an urged [person] is pretty much F'ed and will eventually end up Claimed and totally under the control of the spirit--their free-will a forgotten, discarded shell to the alien intelligence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. That's why spirits want to enter the physical. Of course, there's this big old barrier in the way, and Uratha guarding the border.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1009445#post1009445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because from this perspective nothing in the CofD looks more burn-it-with-fire terrifying than the spirits and the inevitability of their plague on mankind.</div> </div> </div> </div>As well they should! Spirits are fucking terrifying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1009445#post1009445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PS. Ok, the answer can be &amp;quot;Uratha!&amp;quot; and that's why The Wolf must Hunt, sure, but they're relatively few in number and always were.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why the killing of Urfarah was such a controversial decision. He was weakening, but he was still the flesh's best defense against the Shadow. If it weren't for the Gauntlet, it would be an impossible task. So, it's kind of a good thing the border marches were replaced by it. And it's implied that it may have been made by the werewolves to make their job more manageable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T14:31:45-08:00","id":1009481,"title":"","content":"Rank 1 and 2 spirits are more like animals and children. Rank 3 and higher become more like people. Why feudalism? Why risk your neck when you can get someone else to do it for you? Especially when the hisil is littered with loci, which allow them to gorge themselves and maintain their power without doing risky things like reaching across to create a cult.<br /> <br /> As for why every spirit doesn't come across, not every spirit can. Conceptual spirits are the ones most likely to come across, cause their Resonances are often temporary. A Resonance of anger might pop up in a house for an hour and never again. During that time a spirit would need to 'rank up' enough to get all the Influences, numina and manifestations required to cross and make it worth it once they did, since once they're on our side they start bleeding Essence until they get a fetter. It would be great to just jump across but not every spirit has that opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T20:03:12-08:00","id":1009609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1009476#post1009476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Higher Rank spirits find it more difficult to cross the Gauntlet and to exist in the physical world for extended periods of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Higher Rank gives you more Manifestations and more dice to roll, and 2e's done away with the scaling cost of Essence bleed.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, the trouble is that spirits have to manifest to maintain their grip on the material world, they don't exist in a vacuum, and one seldom gets to Rank 5 by camping out and farming a single source of Essence even if there weren't self-evident consequences to locking the resonance of a subject into something suitable for a spirit that's almost certainly not a pure conceptual expression anymore.<br /> <br /> A grove that's host to a Fettered death spirit is going to start to look like a grove that's host to a Fettered death spirit unless deliberate effort is made to conceal those changes, and sooner or later someone or something \u2014 be it werewolf or spirit or mage or mortal occultist \u2014 is going to come calling and kick the hornet's nest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T21:26:15-08:00","id":1009631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1009445#post1009445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because from this perspective nothing in the CofD looks more burn-it-with-fire terrifying than the spirits and the inevitability of their plague on mankind.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Tangenting slightly: this is part of why I love Operation FORT in Hunter: the Vigil. People who have waded far enough out into the cosmic ocean to realize just how deep it is, and all they have are water-wings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T22:19:20-08:00","id":1009640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1009609#post1009609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. Higher Rank gives you more Manifestations and more dice to roll, and 2e's done away with the scaling cost of Essence bleed.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, the trouble is that spirits have to manifest to maintain their grip on the material world, they don't exist in a vacuum, and one seldom gets to Rank 5 by camping out and farming a single source of Essence even if there weren't self-evident consequences to locking the resonance of a subject into something suitable for a spirit that's almost certainly not a pure conceptual expression anymore.<br /> <br /> A grove that's host to a Fettered death spirit is going to start to look like a grove that's host to a Fettered death spirit unless deliberate effort is made to conceal those changes, and sooner or later someone or something \u2014 be it werewolf or spirit or mage or mortal occultist \u2014 is going to come calling and kick the hornet's nest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points, all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T04:13:34-08:00","id":1009716,"title":"","content":"How does a spirit know what to target with it's abilities when it's reaching, since it cannot see what's in the mortal realm while it's in the shadow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T04:28:37-08:00","id":1009721,"title":"","content":"It's never made particularly clear, but my current solution is: They actually <i>can </i>do that.<br /> <br /> My reasoning is thus: The ability that lets werewolves do the same is called <i>spirit senses</i>. Wolf senses give you the senses of a wolf, therefore spirit senses give you the senses of a spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T07:17:27-08:00","id":1009759,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the responses. So still trying to distill the essence (haha) of this, and their ecology. What I gather is:<br /> <br /> * All spirits can perceive the material world, if dimly.<br /> <br /> * All spirits greatly prefer to consume essence of their own flavor. Sorta like an environment where you only eat other people of your own racial and social-economic background, and find the idea of vegetables to be abhorrent if, yes, nourishing in some permanently tainting way.<br /> <br /> * Rank 1-2 spirits are essentially insects in motivations. They eat, they grow, they.. um, &quot;molt&quot; into higher ranks. They greatly prefer to choose the least-risky avenue for essence--a loci if possible, a mote otherwise, and then onward to escalating levels of trouble/danger. This means they can sense danger, and at least understand that everything else could, theoretically, eat them. Their level of social organization is roughly limited to either (warily) ignoring other spirits or intimidating ones of a similar or lesser rank into crapping out a bit of essence in terror (and hoping the stronger one can't catch them after consuming it). Similarly, higher-ranked spirits &quot;squeeze&quot; these guys for a little essence and if in a good mood let them continue to graze. <br /> <br /> * Rank 3+ spirits are more intelligent, more capable of social organization to make their consumption quest efficient, and more empowered to reach across (assuming they can pass the gauntlet). They're also more noticeable and affect the environment around them more, so are concerned by the idea that bigger spirits will find and consume them. Hence a motivation to farm lesser spirits, escape into the material, or join a stable (i.e. feudal) structure so someone will nominally care they still exist.<br /> <br /> * No one likes the fuzz... uzz-y werewolves. Spoilsports. Keeping a good spirit down in Twilight and away from tasty, tasty Man.<br /> <br /> * A self-aware spirit realizes that manifesting is costly, it has to fetter/claim to stabilize itself, and that's a commitment that brings unwanted attention. Particularly bright spirits understand they can just as easily eat themselves out of lunch in the material, but can also easily create the circumstances to make more. Few ponder the consequences on material order that will follow, or the unwanted attention.<br /> <br /> Other than this whistle-stop summary, I still have a major hole--what makes a spirit &quot;hungry&quot;? It burns essence to do things, sure, but if it's hanging in the Hisil, minding its own business, does it lose essence at any rate (similar to vampires, say)? What drives a spirit to hunt other than pure desire to molt into higher, less vulnerable forms? They don't naturally reproduce--fissioning off essence for a new spirit-mote.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm still not seeing why every spirit wouldn't just want at some point to reach across and claim a human if they know there are no Uratha around. Maybe Werewolf is really a giant game of Hawaii Fur-O or Hisil Vice and the fact the police exist is enough to make the spiritual grifters and gangster and punks a tiny bit cautious...? But if you're a butterfly mote, &quot;raised&quot; in an environment without Uratha coming around, who's going to tell you it's a bad idea? Maybe that killjoy spirit who hangs out in the field with you? (The side road is famous for discrete teenage affairs....)<br /> <br /> Trying to put it all together. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T07:24:27-08:00","id":1009769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1009631#post1009631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tangenting slightly: this is part of why I love Operation FORT in Hunter: the Vigil. People who have waded far enough out into the cosmic ocean to realize just how deep it is, and all they have are water-wings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll have to look up Operation FORT.<br /> <br /> There are many things about the CofD that I like better than WoD. Chief among them are that it makes Lovecraftian horror stories write itself, and Werewolves have gone from violent, failed, tree-hugging terrorists to OMGMANSBESTFRIENDBREEDMORENOW!<br /> <br /> That's... a significant shift in tone.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T07:29:45-08:00","id":1009773,"title":"","content":"Spirits lose one essence a day no matter what. Yes, much like vampires. <br /> <br /> Also as well as their own type of essence spirits can also consume spirits of an essence that would make sense for them to eat. A fox spirit can eat rabbit spirits for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T07:41:27-08:00","id":1009784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1009716#post1009716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does a spirit know what to target with it's abilities when it's reaching, since it cannot see what's in the mortal realm while it's in the shadow?</div> </div> </div> </div>It says somewhere in the spirit section that spirits can detect sources of their Resonance within five hundred feet or something. There's a Numina that extends that, I believe it's called Seek.<br /> <br /> Here we go, p184, 'Spirits can sense sources of Essence appropriate for their needs from up to a mile away, even across the Gauntlet without penalty. The &quot;Seek&quot; Numen (p. 193) increases this range.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1009759#post1009759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* All spirits greatly prefer to consume essence of their own flavor. Sorta like an environment where you only eat other people of your own racial and social-economic background, and find the idea of vegetables to be abhorrent if, yes, nourishing in some permanently tainting way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, one becomes a magath, a mad thing that is an outcast among spirits. It's not just of their own flavor, though. A fire spirit can eat a wood spirit, because conceptually a fire can find fuel from wood, just like a predator-spirit like a cat spirits could eat rat, bird, and frog spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Rank 1-2 spirits are essentially insects in motivations. They eat, they grow, they.. um, &quot;molt&quot; into higher ranks. They greatly prefer to choose the least-risky avenue for essence--a loci if possible, a mote otherwise, and then onward to escalating levels of trouble/danger. This means they can sense danger, and at least understand that everything else could, theoretically, eat them. Their level of social organization is roughly limited to either (warily) ignoring other spirits or intimidating ones of a similar or lesser rank into crapping out a bit of essence in terror (and hoping the stronger one can't catch them after consuming it). Similarly, higher-ranked spirits &quot;squeeze&quot; these guys for a little essence and if in a good mood let them continue to graze. </div> </div> </div>Personality-wise, they're comparable to animals and children, it says this in the Rank section. They aren't completely stupid, just single-minded, Rank 2 spirits are often totems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Rank 3+ spirits are more intelligent, more capable of social organization to make their consumption quest efficient, and more empowered to reach across (assuming they can pass the gauntlet). They're also more noticeable and affect the environment around them more, so are concerned by the idea that bigger spirits will find and consume them. Hence a motivation to farm lesser spirits, escape into the material, or join a stable (i.e. feudal) structure so someone will nominally care they still exist. </div> </div> </div>Rank 3 is not about intelligence, it's about independence, personality and depth. At that point a spirit has become more than 'a spirit of rage,' and is likely a spirit of a certain kind of rage, or of something related like rage and fire, and it will act accordingly by trying to cultivate it or find specialized sources of it. Intelligence is something spirits can put on and take off, and isn't the lynchpin of spirit survival the way it can be with humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * No one likes the fuzz... uzz-y werewolves. Spoilsports. Keeping a good spirit down in Twilight and away from tasty, tasty Man. </div> </div> </div>Well, the Pure are alright because they let spirits do what they want. And other spirits can try and take advantage of werewolves, even Forsaken. Some become totems, some manipulate or otherwise force bargains. Not all werewolf packs are capable of destroying all spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * A self-aware spirit realizes that manifesting is costly, it has to fetter/claim to stabilize itself, and that's a commitment that brings unwanted attention. Particularly bright spirits understand they can just as easily eat themselves out of lunch in the material, but can also easily create the circumstances to make more. Few ponder the consequences on material order that will follow, or the unwanted attention. </div> </div> </div>Not just costly, sometimes prohibitive simply by how they've developed. Not all spirits have Fetter. And it's more accurate to say they wouldn't care about the consequences in the gurihal, the meat world. The most intelligent fire spirit in the world would be fine engulfing the entire world in flames if they could make it last. But conceptual spirits often require human action, so need or want human tools.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other than this whistle-stop summary, I still have a major hole--what makes a spirit &quot;hungry&quot;? It burns essence to do things, sure, but if it's hanging in the Hisil, minding its own business, does it lose essence at any rate (similar to vampires, say)? What drives a spirit to hunt other than pure desire to molt into higher, less vulnerable forms? They don't naturally reproduce--fissioning off essence for a new spirit-mote. </div> </div> </div>They're constantly using Essence just to survive, Elfive pointed out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I'm still not seeing why every spirit wouldn't just want at some point to reach across and claim a human if they know there are no Uratha around. Maybe Werewolf is really a giant game of Hawaii Fur-O or Hisil Vice and the fact the police exist is enough to make the spiritual grifters and gangster and punks a tiny bit cautious...? But if you're a butterfly mote, &quot;raised&quot; in an environment without Uratha coming around, who's going to tell you it's a bad idea? Maybe that killjoy spirit who hangs out in the field with you? (The side road is famous for discrete teenage affairs....) </div> </div> </div>Some just can't, as I said, not every spirit gets Fetter or an appropriate way to get across. Werewolves aren't the only possible enemy out there, mortal occultists and other spirits will likely work against them as well. The city spirit doesn't want the fire spirit to burn it down. Plus Reaching across isn't necessary when you can just use Influences to create the Essence you want without risking going over there. Said fire spirit can just find arsonists and Influence them into doing their thing, following them around from across the Gauntlet safely and eating up any competitor fire spirits.<br /> <br /> Some will cross and if lucky become near-immortal Claimed, defeating every werewolf that comes across them. Maybe they'll just make a deal with werewolves, getting them to appreciate they're not worth trying to hunt, maybe they'll just luck out and find someplace without werewolves that never has werewolves passing through or an observant community. Plus while werewolves hunt, not every one is as concerned about claimed or even spirits as they are about other prey. Or maybe they'll become a totem and hunt with the werewolves. They get nice Essence that way too.<br /> <br /> As for how they know, it's been ingrained in them for eons since Father Wolf hunted those who overstepped their bounds, and kept up by some of the most powerful spirits in the Hisil, like Helios and Luna. It's something spirits just know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Added some clarifications with feeding. 11-29-2016, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T09:11:44-08:00","id":1009825,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say werewolves are Spirit Police, nor that a Werewolf game is Hawaii Fur-O (love the names, by the way). This was a vibe that came across pretty strongly in 1E, but is less prominent in 2E, mostly because it has so clearly defined what the Uratha are- the Uratha are <i>predators</i>, the natural apex predators of Flesh and Shadow. Werewolves are part of the spiritual ecology, and in my opinion they act as a keystone species for the Shadow, much as actual wolves do in the real world.<br /> <br /> To quote Wikipedia:<br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;A classic keystone species is a small <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Predator\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0645AD\">predator</span></a> that prevents a particular <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herbivorous\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0645AD\">herbivorous</span></a> species from eliminating dominant <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plant\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0645AD\">plant</span></a> species. Since the prey numbers are low, the keystone predator numbers can be even lower and still be effective. Yet without the predators, the herbivorous prey would explode in numbers, wipe out the dominant plants, and dramatically alter the character of the ecosystem. The exact scenario changes in each example, but the central idea remains that through a chain of interactions, a non-abundant species has an out-sized impact on ecosystem functions.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Let's carry this metaphor through a little bit. So, the Uratha are the small predator, the spirits, collectively, are the herbivorous species, and the entire gurihal (IE. The Flesh/Earth) are the plants- or, to be more specific, the Resonance produced by things in the gurihal are the plants. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> mentions above, a Fire Spirit is only after Fire Resonance. This means they would be more than happy to burn everything to the ground in search of more Essence, but other spirits would protest because burning everything means that the Fire Spirit is directly impacting their own food supply. They respond the same way many species would to their food supply being threatened, increased aggression and retaliation against the competitors. Lions going after hyenas, all that good stuff. This would result in a lot of chaos and collateral damage across the Flesh that wouldn't be desirable, because every single spirit would be doing the exact same thing as that example Fire Spirit, and eventually the spirits would come to some sort of ecological equilibrium, but not before the entire world went to pot. Think of what happened in Yellowstone after the wolf culling in a best case scenario, and what's happening in the Everglades with Burmese Pythons in a worst case scenario.<br /> <br /> Werewolves, then, acting on their instincts as natural predators, deter spirits from becoming super-persistent invasive populations that obliterate everything in their path, mostly by preying upon the ones that isolate themselves- the ones that leave the relative 'safety' of their herds/broods/courts in a hostile environment for a shot at more easily accessible food in an equally (but differently) hostile environment. Sometimes, much like actual predators, instead of doing the smart thing and going after the weak and the isolated, Werewolves go after the strong and healthy, spirits that think more like people (or gods) than animals or children. The death of such a powerful spirit, temporary or otherwise, opens up massive social and ecological niches that such a powerful spirit may have been holding for centuries, even millennia. I think it's even mentioned in the books that the death of a powerful spirit might even result in a mass awakening of spirits of related Resonance as Essence floods the area.<br /> <br /> It's also helpful to think of the Shadow as an environment that recently experienced a mass extinction event. The Sundering only occurred a mere 7,000 years ago, which is the blink of an eye, geologically speaking, and for many spirits this might even count as being within their 'lifetime' or generation. Much like the K-T extinction event, an entire <i>super</i><i>family </i>of spiritual megafauna, the Pangaeans, went extinct, leaving a massive gaping hole in the Shadow's ecology, and spirits are still rushing to fill the gap. Werewolves are kind of like living fossils, the last, adaptable remnant of a much larger biological clade. When the Shadow eventually calms itself back down, which isn't likely to happen for tens of thousands of years, it might end up looking very different. For all we know, it will never calm down, because there are metaphysical and cosmological implications to the Pangaeans and spirits that don't fit into evolutionary or ecological models.</span></span></span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T11:00:39-08:00","id":1009865,"title":"","content":"You are scholars and gentlefolk all. Thanks--knowing spirits lose essence daily, by itself helps a ton! <br /> <br /> So, to follow the analogy--you might actually get little herds of Kodama forest-spirits wandering around waiting for a new sprouting tree to give off that burst of essence. In some kind of communal arrangement. Without the little rattleheads just all eating each other. Because (for example) the Great Forest Spirit set the local order in place and the wolves by nature or arrangement ensure aberrations are pruned.<br /> <br /> With all of this discussion I've been trying to understand how the Hisil functions as an ongoing ecology, because in the books it is easily and often depicted as the realm of terrifying uber-predation into which the Uratha are cautious and Man is fooked. That... has its place. But it's frankly callousing if its the only portrayal available. Arcanist's analogy is particularly helpful as it points to a self-ordering environment that CAN spawn monsters, but doesn't have to and if it does even other spirits will work to return balance.<br /> <br /> And the question of &quot;what arises after the Pangaeans&quot; might not have to wait that long: evolution happens startlingly quickly under environmental and predatory pressures, after all. (E.g. less than 100 years for sea urchin spines to go from short to long to short again in response to predators.) It's hilarious to think of the Uratha as the mammals (?) surviving a spiritual meteor strike.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T11:28:04-08:00","id":1009873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1009865#post1009865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are scholars and gentlefolk all. Thanks--knowing spirits lose essence daily, by itself helps a ton!<br /> <br /> So, to follow the analogy--you might actually get little herds of Kodama forest-spirits wandering around waiting for a new sprouting tree to give off that burst of essence. In some kind of communal arrangement. Without the little rattleheads just all eating each other. Because (for example) the Great Forest Spirit set the local order in place and the wolves by nature or arrangement ensure aberrations are pruned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus this.<br /> <br /> 'Spirits regain one point of Essence per day they are in proximity to any Condition relating to them \u2014 even across the Gauntlet.'<br /> <br /> It can offset the drain for forest-spirits, just living in a forest, which would have the Forest Resonant Condition. Gives them a reason to not go around eating each other and to band together just for self-defense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With all of this discussion I've been trying to understand how the Hisil functions as an ongoing ecology, because in the books it is easily and often depicted as the realm of terrifying uber-predation into which the Uratha are cautious and Man is fooked. That... has its place. But it's frankly callousing if its the only portrayal available. Arcanist's analogy is particularly helpful as it points to a self-ordering environment that CAN spawn monsters, but doesn't have to and if it does even other spirits will work to return balance. </div> </div> </div>It's dangerous to humans because humans are basically bags of Essence who can't really put up much of a defense against spirits, which are pretty powerful even at low Ranks, and often outnumber them. But occultists, whether mages, other supernaturals, or just human ones, have always been able to make deals with spirits. It's a hard thing to start and most people are going to face Breaking Points just acknowledging the existence of the Hisil, but it's an option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the question of &quot;what arises after the Pangaeans&quot; might not have to wait that long: evolution happens startlingly quickly under environmental and predatory pressures, after all. (E.g. less than 100 years for sea urchin spines to go from short to long to short again in response to predators.) It's hilarious to think of the Uratha as the mammals (?) surviving a spiritual meteor strike.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf </div> </div> </div>There are some things living in the void that Pangaea once was, but it's not really conducive to life because there's not much really there. There's no ground, no air. Just mostly empty space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T11:40:13-08:00","id":1009877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1009865#post1009865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's hilarious to think of the Uratha as the mammals (?) surviving a spiritual meteor strike.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in this analogy, werewolves are birds. They are Pangaeans, after all, just as birds are dinosaurs. They are merely an evolutionary branch that is better suited to the post-extinction-event ecosystem. It's spirits that are mammals in this analogy. A group that had previously been mainly prey trying to survive and avoid the notice of the dominant megafauna, but now flourishes and becomes more abundant after the mass extinction event.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T14:45:15-08:00","id":1009945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1009825#post1009825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also helpful to think of the Shadow as an environment that recently experienced a mass extinction event. The Sundering only occurred a mere 7,000 years ago, which is the blink of an eye, geologically speaking, and for many spirits this might even count as being within their 'lifetime' or generation. Much like the K-T extinction event, an entire <i>super</i><i>family </i>of spiritual megafauna, the Pangaeans, went extinct, leaving a massive gaping hole in the Shadow's ecology, and spirits are still rushing to fill the gap. Werewolves are kind of like living fossils, the last, adaptable remnant of a much larger biological clade. When the Shadow eventually calms itself back down, which isn't likely to happen for tens of thousands of years, it might end up looking very different. For all we know, it will never calm down, because there are metaphysical and cosmological implications to the Pangaeans and spirits that don't fit into evolutionary or ecological models.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting way to interpret the impact of the Sundering, and a good one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1009865#post1009865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the question of &quot;what arises after the Pangaeans&quot; might not have to wait that long: evolution happens startlingly quickly under environmental and predatory pressures, after all. (E.g. less than 100 years for sea urchin spines to go from short to long to short again in response to predators.) It's hilarious to think of the Uratha as the mammals (?) surviving a spiritual meteor strike.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOne potential answer to 'what arises after the Pangaeans?' is to look at what might happen to Uratha when they surpass Primal Urge 10.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1009873#post1009873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's no ground, no air. Just mostly empty space.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis is... not <i>exactly </i>true. I mean, fundamentally no-one really knows what is 'in' the Gauntlet as it's not generally possible to get 'in' to it; glimpses of things when passing through don't really equate to a true experience of the Gauntlet itself.<br /> <br /> \u200bMind you, there's all those rumours, like what the Azlu might be building where they've thickened the Gauntlet enough, or what the Beshilu find when they're gnawing tunnels into it...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T15:08:08-08:00","id":1009956,"title":"","content":"I don't know how relevant it is in 2E, but pages 61-62 in Summoners (a Mage supplement) has a brief description of the inside of the Gauntlet as well as a spell that allows people to look inside it. It even has a sample creature that naturally inhabits the Gauntlet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":".  Spelling 11-29-2016, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T09:57:02-08:00","id":1010237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1009945#post1009945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is an interesting way to interpret the impact of the Sundering, and a good one.<br /> <br /> \u200bOne potential answer to 'what arises after the Pangaeans?' is to look at what might happen to Uratha when they surpass Primal Urge 10.<br /> <br /> \u200bThis is... not <i>exactly </i>true. I mean, fundamentally no-one really knows what is 'in' the Gauntlet as it's not generally possible to get 'in' to it; glimpses of things when passing through don't really equate to a true experience of the Gauntlet itself.<br /> <br /> \u200bMind you, there's all those rumours, like what the Azlu might be building where they've thickened the Gauntlet enough, or what the Beshilu find when they're gnawing tunnels into it...</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank-you sir! Wait, when they <i>surpass </i>Primal Urge 10? Is this another one of those bodhisattva predator references you make every so often, or is this something else?<br /> <br /> And, in regards to the Gauntlet/Border Marches, isn't there references to what people see when they pass through it, seeing as it takes several seconds?<br /> <br /> Ah, found it. <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken Second Edition pg.72</b> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">Some Uratha tell tales about encountering bizarre entities inside the Gauntlet \u2014 ghostly \u201cspirits,\u201d unnatural corpses of no known creature, splashes of blood, and other signs that the barrier is somehow inhabited, always just on the edge of the paralyzed traveler\u2019s senses. Some Cahalith say that when the Sundering rent the Border Marches apart, anything trapped inside was changed as well. </span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1009877#post1009877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in this analogy, werewolves are birds. They are Pangaeans, after all, just as birds are dinosaurs. They are merely an evolutionary branch that is better suited to the post-extinction-event ecosystem. It's spirits that are mammals in this analogy. A group that had previously been mainly prey trying to survive and avoid the notice of the dominant megafauna, but now flourishes and becomes more abundant after the mass extinction event.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the way I was thinking. Post K-T extinction, there were still a decent amount of large, flightless birds that acted as some serious predators until some more adaptable mammals out-competed them, and if you're going by the numbers, birds (IE. dinosaurs) are <i>still </i>more successful and diverse than mammals became- which bodes well for werewolves, if the analogy holds.<br /> <br /> It also helps that Uratha are equal parts Wolf, Human, and Spirit. Two of those three categories are hyper-adaptable opportunistic eusocial persistence predators that spread like weeds wherever they're allowed to reproduce, and the third is an immortal reflection of the world with no choice but to be totally what it is. Seriously, wolves used to be freaking <i>everywhere </i>and humans are, well, humans, and that's tethered to an urge to not just be a hunter, but to <i>\u200bexcel </i>at being a hunter in a way that no purely physical predator would ever even attempt.<br /> <br /> Who knows what werewolves, or even the Shadow, will become in time. Hmm... I have further ideas about Spirit ecology that need to marinate. I'll be back with a big thing later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 11-30-2016, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T11:47:00-08:00","id":1010284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1010237#post1010237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the way I was thinking. Post K-T extinction, there were still a decent amount of large, flightless birds that acted as some serious predators until some more adaptable mammals out-competed them, and if you're going by the numbers, birds (IE. dinosaurs) are <i>still </i>more successful and diverse than mammals became- which bodes well for werewolves, if the analogy holds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. It's also worth noting that werewolves might not be the only Pangaeans that survived the extinction. Azlu and Bishelu might be the remnants of Spider and Rat, just as werewolves are the remnants of Wolf. And we've seen that they are not the only Hosts either. There may still be a great deal of &quot;bio&quot;-diversity among Pangaeans in the modern era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T12:03:15-08:00","id":1010292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1010284#post1010284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. It's also worth noting that werewolves might not be the only Pangaeans that survived the extinction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves aren't Pangaeans \u2014 they're a markedly more unusual crossbreed/creation Luna engineered with Urfarah that were most stable in the Border Marches and developed a cultural focus on carrying on the duties of Wolf, but the Uratha don't have much of any of the qualities that exemplify a Pangaean besides being fleshy creatures with spiritual power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T12:11:34-08:00","id":1010296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1010292#post1010292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves aren't Pangaeans \u2014 they're a markedly more unusual crossbreed/creation Luna engineered with Urfarah that were most stable in the Border Marches and developed a cultural focus on carrying on the duties of Wolf, but the Uratha don't have much of any of the qualities that exemplify a Pangaean besides being fleshy creatures with spiritual power.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not Pangaeans in a literal sense, no. But in the context of a metaphor wherein Pangaeans are dinosaurs and the sundering is the KT mass extinction, they are not unlike birds, which from a taxonomic perspective are a kind of dinosaur. And while evolutionary biology doesn't really apply to spirit-beings, werewolves could be seen as an &quot;evolutionary&quot; offshoot of Pangaeans, just as aves are an evolutionary offshoot of theropods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-30-2016, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T12:52:05-08:00","id":1010315,"title":"","content":"They're not Pangeans, but they are Pangaean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T14:47:52-08:00","id":1010349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1010237#post1010237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank-you sir! Wait, when they <i>surpass </i>Primal Urge 10? Is this another one of those bodhisattva predator references you make every so often, or is this something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bDunno yet, I'll get back to you if/when a 2e Forsaken book covers it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, in regards to the Gauntlet/Border Marches, isn't there references to what people see when they pass through it, seeing as it takes several seconds?<br /> <br /> Ah, found it. <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken Second Edition pg.72</b> Some Uratha tell tales about encountering bizarre entities inside the Gauntlet \u2014 ghostly \u201cspirits,\u201d unnatural corpses of no known creature, splashes of blood, and other signs that the barrier is somehow inhabited, always just on the edge of the paralyzed traveler\u2019s senses. Some Cahalith say that when the Sundering rent the Border Marches apart, anything trapped inside was changed as well. </div> </div> </div>Indeed, hence why I said 'glimpses of things when passing through don't really equate to a true experience of the Gauntlet itself.' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T15:14:29-08:00","id":1010360,"title":"","content":"One thing to add to the extinction metaphor is Humanity. I mean, it's not just the spirits that have proliferated. Humans have overrun the world follwing the Sundering. They both reinforce the Gauntlet with the amount of essence they create and also generate whole new kinds of spirits whilst radically altering those spirits that already exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T16:37:20-08:00","id":1010397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1010360#post1010360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to add to the extinction metaphor is Humanity. I mean, it's not just the spirits that have proliferated. Humans have overrun the world follwing the Sundering. They both reinforce the Gauntlet with the amount of essence they create and also generate whole new kinds of spirits whilst radically altering those spirits that already exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, so I guess that would make humans the mammals and spirits... reptiles? It's not a perfect analogy, but it's definitely interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T08:14:05-08:00","id":1023285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1009865#post1009865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the question of &quot;what arises after the Pangaeans&quot; ?</div> </div> </div> </div>You ask? Why Idigam, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T19:53:56-08:00","id":1024072,"title":"","content":"This is less scholarly than the excellent contributions thus far, but I tend to explain to newer players trying to grok the Shadow that spirits aren't all predators, but they're all <i>addicts</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T04:46:41-08:00","id":1024227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1024072#post1024072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is less scholarly than the excellent contributions thus far, but I tend to explain to newer players trying to grok the Shadow that spirits aren't all predators, but they're all <i>addicts</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Add obsession-compulsion and monomania to that, and most people get why spirits are not good to one's well-being, and are quite different from the spirits from other works of fiction, and why the hell would anyone think the presence of monstrous shapeshifters is not that bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T11:28:21-08:00","id":1024418,"title":"","content":"In reference to what makes a spirit hungry, as others have said a spirit requires 1 essance per day to survive. But they could get that by camping where there is resonance so why 'hunt' for essance? Well, many awakened spirits don't simply sustain themselves on the bare minimum like their slumbering brethren. Usage of some numina, of manifestation or of influences in the pursuit of self preservation or in the search of essance, more often than not cost essance. So spirits seek essance for two main reasons in my opinion, 1)to ensure they don't starve and go dormant - becoming easy prey and 2) so they may grow stronger and as you said &quot;molt&quot; into a higher ranked spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","user":"Mr.F.I.X.","date":".  Prey isnt spelt with an a, oops 12-30-2016, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T20:25:05-08:00","id":1024609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1024418#post1024418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In reference to what makes a spirit hungry, as others have said a spirit requires 1 essance per day to survive. But they could get that by camping where there is resonance so why 'hunt' for essance?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the big reasons is that higher-Ranked spirits tend to charge rent from lower-Ranked spirits and the Shadow caps the two means of gaining Essence that aren't theft at one go per day. Getting a daily n+1 points of Essence from camping at a single source doesn't do you much good when the local apex predator and their subordinates collective charge n-3 points per day on average and you're losing a point per day on basic upkeep besides, which brings us to the next issue:<br /> <br /> Equally-Ranked spirits are going to be looking for a leg up on their fellows, and while taking your sources of Essence doesn't allow them to feed more in itself, subordinating you? Does. This competition gets more intense in environments where multiple powerful spirits are all demanding tribute from their lessers.<br /> <br /> The lack of a cap on theft means spirits who get how the game works recognize that other spirits of compatible resonance are more useful to them alive than dead, and feeding other spirits their Essence makes them closer to extensions of the spirit-lord. Beings like Dihir are basically ecological feedback loops that use smaller spirits as agents of large-scale attempts at resource-control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T20:58:37-08:00","id":1024619,"title":"","content":"Well said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T12:59:19-08:00","id":1024875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1024418#post1024418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In reference to what makes a spirit hungry, as others have said a spirit requires 1 ess<b>E</b>nce per day to survive. But they could get that by camping where there is resonance so why 'hunt' for ess<b>E</b>nce? Well, many awakened spirits don't simply sustain themselves on the bare minimum like their slumbering brethren. Usage of some numina, of manifestation or of influences in the pursuit of self preservation or in the search of ess<b>E</b>nce, more often than not cost ess<b>E</b>nce. So spirits seek ess<b>E</b>nce for two main reasons in my opinion, 1)to ensure they don't starve and go dormant - becoming easy prey and 2) so they may grow stronger and as you said &quot;molt&quot; into a higher ranked spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasys mine, good points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T14:12:15-08:00","id":1024897,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12191_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12191\" data-vbnamecard=\"12191\">Malus</a> well at least I'm consistent haha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T11:26:04-08:00","id":1026068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1024609#post1024609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the big reasons is that higher-Ranked spirits tend to charge rent from lower-Ranked spirits and the Shadow caps the two means of gaining Essence that aren't theft at one go per day. Getting a daily n+1 points of Essence from camping at a single source doesn't do you much good when the local apex predator and their subordinates collective charge n-3 points per day on average and you're losing a point per day on basic upkeep besides, which brings us to the next issue:<br /> <br /> Equally-Ranked spirits are going to be looking for a leg up on their fellows, and while taking your sources of Essence doesn't allow them to feed more in itself, subordinating you? Does. This competition gets more intense in environments where multiple powerful spirits are all demanding tribute from their lessers.<br /> <br /> The lack of a cap on theft means spirits who get how the game works recognize that other spirits of compatible resonance are more useful to them alive than dead, and <b>feeding other spirits their Essence makes them closer to extensions of the spirit-lord.</b> Beings like Dihir are basically ecological feedback loops that use smaller spirits as agents of large-scale attempts at resource-control.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Emphasis mine.)<br /> <br /> Ok, so paying dues to the local Lion King means you get protection and he doesn't accidentally eat you (or your flock of spirit-buds). Subordinating your spirit-buds so they recognize you as the righteous dude who keeps the Lion King at bay means you get some grift. Roman-era tax collection at its finest. Everyone may hate you but you're in with the boss ... until he gets hungry.<br /> <br /> But what's this that I've bolded? Larger spirits feed essence to their &quot;vassal&quot; (my words)? Ok... sounds like a bribe, but:<br /> <br /> How extensively might that change them over time? Would that shift the hyena-spirit into a hyena-lion spirit and eventually a lion-hyena spirit? I get that amalgams result from unrestrained consumption of essence not of the same type, and that that tends to give said spirit a bad name around the block. But the idea of actually force-feeding lesser spirits as flocks is... well, as disturbing as anything around them I suppose?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T12:54:37-08:00","id":1026123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1026068#post1026068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what's this that I've bolded? Larger spirits feed essence to their &quot;vassal&quot; (my words)? Ok... sounds like a bribe, but:</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits literally can't do you a favor unless you pay them with gathra and they are what they eat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How extensively might that change them over time? </div> </div> </div>Not very extensively, after accounting for degrees of remove and compatible resonance \u2014 if a Jaggling claims tithes from a Gaffling, it does so because that Gaffling holds Essence that is palatable to the Jaggling, and this applies the same to the Incarna that the Jaggling pays fealty to. A greater affinity develops along this connection, and this demonstrates itself in the symbolism of the spirits' Corpus \u2014 spirits' forms get larger and more elaborate with Rank for a reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would that shift the hyena-spirit into a hyena-lion spirit and eventually a lion-hyena spirit? I get that amalgams result from unrestrained consumption of essence not of the same type, and that that tends to give said spirit a bad name around the block. </div> </div> </div>It's more that the hyena-servants of a spirit of lions and hyenas start to become hyena spirits that look like they'd serve a spirit of lions and hyenas, which probably has a portfolio that makes that fit more naturally if it isn't a magath.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the idea of actually force-feeding lesser spirits as flocks is... well, as disturbing as anything around them I suppose? </div> </div> </div>It's how the vampires do it, broadly speaking.<br /> <br /> The boss takes a cut from everyone down the chain and gives their subordinates the stuff from their personal stash. Their subordinates do the same for their subordinates, and so on down the line so that every intermediate boss between the bottom and the top is a little more alike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T08:31:14-08:00","id":1027048,"title":"","content":"Hey so I've got a question concerning Motes: Since all spirits start out as motes, what would the mote of an higher animal spirit look like? Would it look like a baby newborn version of the animal, or would it look like a tiny ball of animal components (like a bird spirit mote might be a small bundle of feathers and eyes or a beak or something)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T08:47:10-08:00","id":1027057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nuwisha Nutjob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1027048#post1027048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey so I've got a question concerning Motes: Since all spirits start out as motes, what would the mote of an higher animal spirit look like? Would it look like a baby newborn version of the animal, or would it look like a tiny ball of animal components (like a bird spirit mote might be a small bundle of feathers and eyes or a beak or something)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean Essence or Rank 0 spirits?<br /> <br /> First edition says this about Essence. 'Essence cannot be perceived as a thing in and of itself, but as a series of phenomena. Uratha have to use all of their senses to find free Essence as it bleeds through the Gauntlet and flickers into and out of existence in the spirit world - briefly appearing as sensations related to its resonance. Essence flavored with joy might appear as a whirlwind of flower petals, the sound of laughter, the scent of ice cream, the touch of satin. Essence might appear as each of these sensations to different beings at once.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T11:27:00-08:00","id":1027172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nuwisha Nutjob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1008606-trouble-with-spirits?p=1027048#post1027048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey so I've got a question concerning Motes: Since all spirits start out as motes, what would the mote of an higher animal spirit look like? Would it look like a baby newborn version of the animal, or would it look like a tiny ball of animal components (like a bird spirit mote might be a small bundle of feathers and eyes or a beak or something)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most low-Ranking animal spirits are going to resemble vague and abstracted shapes of their hosts \u2014 a bird-<i>muthra</i> might be little more than a rough-sketched pair of wings in the air, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T11:16:58-08:00","id":1027766,"title":"","content":"Thanks nofather and Satchel. That answer my question. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}